DTSTART:20260917T125200Z
DTEND:20260917T130200Z
SUMMARY:Keynote: A New Way To Build Software: How GitHub Is Evolving For a Human\, Agent Future - Marlene Mhangami\, Senior Developer Advocate\, Microsoft
DESCRIPTION:AI Agents are contributing a growing amount of code to GitHub. Some developers are leaning into this\, creating automated development pipelines\, assigning issues from Slack or changing their review process to be agent first. Other developers\, particularly in open source\, are being overwhelmed by agent generated PR's and issues and are not sure what this means for the future of their project. GitHub is a tool at the center of the software development process and has been evolving quickly for the agentic era. In this talk we'll look at some of the key changes that are here in GitHub and what's to come in the future.
CATEGORIES:KEYNOTE SESSIONS
LOCATION:Auditorium (Ground Floor)\, Amsterdam\, Netherlands
SEQUENCE:0
UID:4c6e214e5b3874b7b3c16e12295d160f
URL:http://agntconmcpconeu26.sched.com/event/4c6e214e5b3874b7b3c16e12295d160f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20260924T215840Z
DTSTART:20260917T130400Z
DTEND:20260917T131400Z
SUMMARY:Keynote: Inside AI Agents -- Offloading Human Tasks - Maarten Grootendorst\, Creator of BERTopic\, KeyBERT & PolyFuzz\, Member of Technical Staff - Google DeepMind
DESCRIPTION:This keynote will cover the foundation of what makes an AI Agents (a reasoning LLM\, memory\, tooling\, and planning) and how the transition into an era of Agentic AI is reflected in the development of LLMs.\nUsing Gemma 3 and Gemma 4\, Maarten will explore how Agentic capabilities in LLMs needed to be prompted in earlier generations (Gemma 3) but became part of the core behavior in later generations (Gemma 4).\n
CATEGORIES:KEYNOTE SESSIONS
LOCATION:Auditorium (Ground Floor)\, Amsterdam\, Netherlands
SEQUENCE:0
UID:9863191944bad057ff0377ffbf2051ca
URL:http://agntconmcpconeu26.sched.com/event/9863191944bad057ff0377ffbf2051ca
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20260924T215840Z
DTSTART:20260917T131600Z
DTEND:20260917T132600Z
SUMMARY:Keynote: Why Organizations Need an AI Control Plane for Security and Governance - Sheng Liang\, Co-Founder & CEO\, Obot AI
DESCRIPTION:How can organizations secure and govern AI agents they do not fully trust? MCP gateways can intercept and filter tool calls\, but that alone is not enough. Organizations also need complete visibility into agent activity\, consistent policy enforcement\, and centralized control. In this talk\, we explain how to move beyond MCP gateways and build an AI control plane for enterprise-wide security and governance.
CATEGORIES:KEYNOTE SESSIONS
LOCATION:Auditorium (Ground Floor)\, Amsterdam\, Netherlands
SEQUENCE:0
UID:153562e35e20f47bf2acb1a157ec089a
URL:http://agntconmcpconeu26.sched.com/event/153562e35e20f47bf2acb1a157ec089a
